      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1878, Challis was designated the capital of Custer County, a move that helped it survive early mining boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kupi.com/en/explore/united-states/challis/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits in Round Valley, a geographic hub that made it a logistics center for gold miners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kupi.com/en/explore/united-states/challis/history",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A massive gold dredge once operated on the Yankee Fork, and the site remains a notable historic landmark.",
